Parliament committees have heard and  questioned viraja Rover vice-president  designates in charge of values and  transparency and Joseph Burrell the  union's High Representative for Foreign  Affairs and security policy Vera der  over from Czechia is the nominee for the  values and transparency portfolio my  goal will be to make Europe more  democratic and transparent to make  Europe more resilient against new  threats including digital ones and to  make Europe more capable of defending  the values we cherish including the rule  of law and media freedom until now she  was Commissioner for justice consumers  and gender equality the lawyer and  businesswoman was heard by MEP s from  the constitutional affairs and civil  liberties committees they questioned her  position on the rule of law and tangible  consequences for countries that threaten  it Independence of judiciary issues  freedom of expression and freedom of  association  Joseph Burrell has been nominated as the  union's High Representative for Foreign  Affairs and security policy sitting as  vice presidents of the Commission and  chairing the Council of Ministers for  Foreign Affairs the Spanish Foreign  Affairs Minister is a former presidents  of the European Parliament speaking to  members of the Foreign Affairs Committee  Borel said that in an increasingly  turbulent world Europe needs to be more  assertive we should pull our national  sovereignties together to multiply the  power of individual member states and I  am convinced that we don't act together  Europe will become irrelevant mep x'  wanted to know how he'd encourage  european unity his position on threats  to the rule of law and human rights in  countries across the world and on  relations with key players such as china  or the US  the vote in parliament to decided the  commission as a whole is accepted or  rejected is scheduled for the 23rd of  October
 

